#. Tag: title
#: techinfo.docbook:11
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kword; file format"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: techinfo.docbook:12
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kword;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: techinfo.docbook:12
#, no-c-format
msgid "file format"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: techinfo.docbook:14
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; uses two open source, independently developed standards for its file "
"format. The combination was chosen for its balance between convenience and "
"open development models."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: techinfo.docbook:18
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"First, it should be noted that all &kword; files are multiple &XML; files "
"that are compressed to reduce their space requirements."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: techinfo.docbook:21
#, no-c-format
msgid "Select the &kword; version you are interested in:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: techinfo.docbook:23
#, no-c-format
msgid "<link linkend=\"kword-file-format-11\">&kword; 1.1 and earlier</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: techinfo.docbook:24
#, no-c-format
msgid "<link linkend=\"kword-file-format-12\">&kword; 1.2</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: techinfo.docbook:25
#, no-c-format
msgid "<link linkend=\"kword-file-format-13\">&kword; 1.3</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: techinfo.docbook:30
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kword; 1.1 and earlier"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: techinfo.docbook:32
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &XML; files are compressed into a single file using the same algorithm "
"as used by <ulink url=\"http://www.gnu.org/software/tar/tar.html"
"\"><application>tar</application></ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: techinfo.docbook:36 techinfo.docbook:99 techinfo.docbook:173
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can uncompress the files with the following command:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: techinfo.docbook:38
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>%</prompt> <userinput><command>tar -xzvf </"
"command><replaceable>filename</replaceable></userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: techinfo.docbook:40 techinfo.docbook:103 techinfo.docbook:177
#, no-c-format
msgid "This will expand the &kword; document file into its component files."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: techinfo.docbook:43 techinfo.docbook:106 techinfo.docbook:180
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The text portion of all &kword; files are &XML; (eXtensible Markup Language) "
"files."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: techinfo.docbook:46
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For more information on &XML; documents, processors and technology, please "
"visit"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: ulink
#: techinfo.docbook:48 techinfo.docbook:111 techinfo.docbook:185
#, no-c-format
msgid "World Wide Web Consortium &XML; pages"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: ulink
#: techinfo.docbook:50 techinfo.docbook:113 techinfo.docbook:187
#, no-c-format
msgid "XML.org Resource Guide"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: ulink
#: techinfo.docbook:51 techinfo.docbook:114 techinfo.docbook:188
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &XML; FAQ"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: techinfo.docbook:54
#, no-c-format
msgid "All &kword; documents consist of at least two &XML; files:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: techinfo.docbook:58 techinfo.docbook:121 techinfo.docbook:195
#, no-c-format
msgid "maindoc.xml"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: techinfo.docbook:60
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This file contains the bulk of the &kword; text, tables and formula "
"information. It is marked with &XML; tags according to the official DTD. A "
"copy of the &kword; 1.1 DTD is located at: <ulink url=\"http://www.koffice."
"org/DTD/kword-1.1.dtd\">http://www.koffice.org/DTD/kword-1.1.dtd</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: techinfo.docbook:67 techinfo.docbook:130 techinfo.docbook:204
#, no-c-format
msgid "documentinfo.xml"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: techinfo.docbook:69
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This file contains the document information. This is information entered "
"into the dialog boxes when selecting <menuchoice><guimenu>File</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Document Information</guimenuitem> </menuchoice> from "
"the menubar. This information is useful for tracking authors, contact "
"information &etc;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: techinfo.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The DTD for &koffice; 1.1 is located at: <ulink url=\"http://www.koffice.org/"
"DTD/document-info-1.1.dtd\">http://www.koffice.org/DTD/document-info-1.1."
"dtd</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: techinfo.docbook:80 techinfo.docbook:154 techinfo.docbook:228
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In addition, there may be other files included in the &kword; document file. "
"Pictures, embedded documents and other binary information are stored within "
"the &kword; document as separate files."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: techinfo.docbook:84 techinfo.docbook:158 techinfo.docbook:232
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For more specific information on &kword; file storage or other internal "
"information, please see <ulink url=\"http://www.koffice.org/developer\">The "
"KOffice API</ulink> and the <ulink url=\"http://developer.kde.org\">General "
"&kde; developer information pages</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: techinfo.docbook:92
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kword; 1.2"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: techinfo.docbook:94 techinfo.docbook:168
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The text files are compressed into a single file using the same algorithm as "
"used by <ulink url=\"http://www.info-zip.org/pub/infozip/Zip.html"
"\"><application>zip</application></ulink>. This change was made because of "
"its broad use in other open source office suites and its improved "
"performance with lower memory requirements."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: techinfo.docbook:101 techinfo.docbook:175
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>%</prompt> <userinput><command>unzip </"
"command><replaceable>filename</replaceable></userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: techinfo.docbook:109 techinfo.docbook:183
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For more information on &XML; documents, processing and technology, please "
"visit"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: techinfo.docbook:117 techinfo.docbook:191
#, no-c-format
msgid "All &kword; documents consist of at least three files:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: techinfo.docbook:123 techinfo.docbook:197
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This file contains the bulk of the &kword; text, tables and formula "
"information. It is marked with &XML; tags according to the official DTD."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: techinfo.docbook:125
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A copy of the &kword; 1.2 DTD is located at: <ulink url=\"http://www.koffice."
"org/DTD/kword-1.2.dtd\">http://www.koffice.org/DTD/kword-1.2.dtd</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: techinfo.docbook:132 techinfo.docbook:206
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This file contains the document information. This is information entered "
"into the dialog boxes when selecting <menuchoice><guimenu>File</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Document Information</guimenuitem> </menuchoice> from "
"the menubar. This information is useful for tracking authors, contact "
"information etc."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: techinfo.docbook:137
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The DTD for &koffice; 1.2 is located at: <ulink url=\"http://www.koffice.org/"
"DTD/document-info-1.2.dtd\">http://koffice.kde.org/DTD/document-info-1.2."
"dtd</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: techinfo.docbook:143 techinfo.docbook:217
#, no-c-format
msgid "mimetype"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: techinfo.docbook:145 techinfo.docbook:219
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This file contains the mimetype for &kword; files. This information is used "
"by &kde; to determine that this is a &kword; file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: techinfo.docbook:147 techinfo.docbook:221
#, no-c-format
msgid "This file always contains: <emphasis>application/x-kword</emphasis>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: techinfo.docbook:166
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kword; 1.3 (current version)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: techinfo.docbook:199
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A copy of the &kword; 1.3 DTD is located at: <ulink url=\"http://www.koffice."
"org/DTD/kword-1.3.dtd\">http://www.koffice.org/DTD/kword-1.3.dtd</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: techinfo.docbook:211
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The DTD for &koffice; 1.3 is located at: <ulink url=\"http://www.koffice.org/"
"DTD/document-info-1.3.dtd\">http://koffice.kde.org/DTD/document-info-1.3."
"dtd</ulink>."
msgstr ""
